1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,236
Where does your stop go? Five legends, two camps.

2
00:00:04,237 --> 00:00:09,599
Your stop: the price where you sell and take a small loss.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:14,765
Livermore watched how a stock acted after he bought.

4
00:00:14,766 --> 00:00:20,389
O'Neil used a fixed line: a small loss, every time.

5
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:25,098
Darvas set his stop the moment he bought.

6
00:00:25,099 --> 00:00:30,722
Kovner went wider, and bought less to pay for it.

7
00:00:30,723 --> 00:00:33,599
Seykota kept it short.

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,974
Camp one: a fixed percent below your buy.

9
00:00:37,975 --> 00:00:43,199
Camp two: just under the range it broke out of.

10
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:48,203
Where they all agree: decide the exit before you buy.

11
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:52,799
Keep the loss small. And when it hits, go.

12
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:57,174
Pick the price that proves your idea wrong.

13
00:00:57,175 --> 00:01:02,399
Too far away? Buy fewer shares, like in Lore 005.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,549
Lore 007. Next: Lore 008, Expectancy in 15 seconds
